# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) if you need to override a default.
#
# Expo CLI loads `.env*` from THIS directory — the Expo project root — not from the repo root.
# Everything here is public by construction: the `EXPO_PUBLIC_` prefix means Expo inlines the
# value into the JavaScript bundle at build time, where any user can read it in DevTools.
# **Never put a credential behind that prefix.** If something needs a key, it goes through the
# Worker. See docs/10 "Configuration & secrets" — and `.env.example` at the repo root, which is the
# inventory of every variable in the repo — for the full picture.

# Base URL of the edge Worker. Defaults to `DEFAULT_API_URL` in `@nextbus/api-client`
# (http://localhost:8787) when unset, which is what `pnpm dev` serves. Set it to the deployed Worker
# for a real build — `build:web` bakes it into both the bundle and the service worker's
# runtime-caching routes (ADR-058). The `/v1/live` socket URL is **derived** from this one value
# (`liveSocketUrl`, ADR-056 decision 8), so this stays the only line to change for a real domain.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8787

# The socket, both read since WP5-6 (ADR-076). `LIVE_TRANSPORT` is `poll` (the default) or `socket`;
# there is no `auto`, and an unrecognised value falls back to `poll` with a warning. `LIVE_URL` is the
# escape hatch for a socket tier on a different host — unset means it is derived from the API URL above:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_LIVE_URL=wss://live.example.test/v1/live
# EXPO_PUBLIC_LIVE_TRANSPORT=poll
